TIP:  The second option for the intro includes the 4 piano notes (which may or may not transpose).  If untransposed they can all be played from within the strum of (G).  Strum (G) and then pick the open 2nd string twice, then the open 3rd string once, now drop (or flatten) your index finger out so it covers the 3rd string and pick it once, lift off and pick the 3rd string again.  Resume strumming the (G).    

TIP:  (Cadd9) comes between two (C) chords so keep the (C) form and add pinky to 2nd string/3rd fret.  And try to wrap your thumb over the top string/2nd fret on the last (D) in the verse.	
   

